A port named Kosmos (docs/w6.md W6a). WebKit's CMake refuses a PORT it
does not list, so Kosmos joins the list; and BUILDING_KOSMOS__, which
OptionsKosmos.cmake defines, gives PLATFORM(KOSMOS) and BPLATFORM(KOSMOS)
as GTK's and WPE's do. On a Mac, WebKit looks for an Apple SDK before
anything else, whatever it builds for - JSCOnly's build found the macOS
one and never used it - and a Kosmos build is never for an Apple
platform, so it does not look. The port's own files - its options, WTF's
sources - are Kosmos's, in runtime/ports/webkit/Source.

diff -ruN a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-11-13 09:06:54.349144506 -0300
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-11-13 09:06:54.365849185 -0300
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.20)
 set(CMAKE_MODULE_PATH "${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}/Source/cmake")
 
-if (CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Darwin")
+if (CMAKE_HOST_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "Darwin" AND NOT PORT STREQUAL "Kosmos")
     # Resolve the SDK and pin tools before the call to project().
     include(WebKitXcodeSDK)
 endif ()
